READJH orchestrates and distills rules from the following upstream works.
It does not vendor their code; the executors are invoked from their own
installs, and the distilled rules in references/ carry per-section attribution.

Executable skills (pointer contract, invoked from the user's machine):

  readme-crafter-skill
    Repo:    https://github.com/linhai0872/readme-crafter-skill
    Author:  linhai (linhai0872)
    License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 linhai

  writing-humanize (part of ink-and-agency)
    Repo:    https://github.com/risadams/ink-and-agency (skills/writing-humanize/)
    Author:  Ris Adams <ris@risadams.com>
    License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Ris Adams; repo LICENSE notes the repo is
             a fork/adaptation of https://github.com/mattpocock/skills
    READJH suppresses two upstream behaviors when invoking this skill —
    self-evolve journaling and personality injection (see UPSTREAM.md).

Distilled rule sources (subsets distilled into references/, never invoked):

  sepia
    Repo:    no canonical public upstream recorded; local mirror at
             .agents/skills/sepia/ (authoring machine)
    Author:  not recorded in the mirror (SKILL.md carries license: MIT,
             no author field)
    License: MIT (SKILL.md frontmatter)

  anti-defensive-writing (English variant)
    Repo:    https://github.com/Kiterlin/anti-defensive-writing
    Author:  Kiterlin
    License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Kiterlin
    Note:    a same-named source exists elsewhere; READJH distills only the
             Kiterlin variant, referenced by path (ADR-0001, UPSTREAM.md).

  academic-humanizer
    Repo:    https://github.com/AIScientists-Dev/academic-humanizer
